{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1111558-skin-dancer-homeland","id":1111558,"title":"Skin Dancer Homeland","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-04T22:21:54-07:00","id":1111558,"title":"Skin Dancer Homeland","content":"As the skin dancers are all a small tribe and every tribe has a tribal homeland according to the w20 velvet shadow book,i wanted to ask you all. What do you guys think this very fledgeling little realm would look like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T07:44:43-07:00","id":1111656,"title":"","content":"Ed Gein's spare room.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T10:48:34-07:00","id":1111713,"title":"","content":"A roofless labyrinth, naked below a moonless sky filled with strange old stars. Sometimes the walls are unyielding granite, or marble covered in grotesque reliefs, or densely packed vines covered in jagged thorns. Sometimes it is sinew and sweaty flesh. Some say there are pathways through this maze to other places in the Umbra, but all of them are dark and terrible.<br /> <br /> A few of the spirits that walk the maze are lost, trapped in Minotaur's domain. These unfortunate beings provide meals for the twisted totem and his children. Others are kindred spirits to the Man-Beast, chimeric horrors that might have been something akin to Ancestor spirits in a more wholesome tribe. They are tainted and often mad, but they often know secrets spurned by Gaian souls. They can also bestow their gifts on those found worthy, with offerings of blood, skin, and bone being the common currency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T10:56:30-07:00","id":1111717,"title":"","content":"Would this be a separate realm, or a corrupted version of the original White Howler tribal homeland?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T11:05:53-07:00","id":1111720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1111558-skin-dancer-homeland?p=1111717#post1111717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would this be a separate realm, or a corrupted version of the original White Howler tribal homeland?</div> </div> </div> </div>This may have changed with the newer versions but isn't important the Skindancers AREN'T Wyrm tainted?<br /> <br /> They're murderers but not servants of the Great Enemy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T11:16:27-07:00","id":1111725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1111558-skin-dancer-homeland?p=1111720#post1111720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This may have changed with the newer versions but isn't important the Skindancers AREN'T Wyrm tainted?<br /> <br /> They're murderers but not servants of the Great Enemy.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are wyrm tainted unless the kinfolk conducts the rite with 5 skins intentionally given by the Garou. It isn't likely to happen at all, but it seems almost unheard of for it to be done in a Gaia-pleasing way. Most skindancers are tainted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T12:04:36-07:00","id":1111760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1111558-skin-dancer-homeland?p=1111720#post1111720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This may have changed with the newer versions but isn't important the Skindancers AREN'T Wyrm tainted?<br /> <br /> They're murderers but not servants of the Great Enemy.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are very much wyrmtainted, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3695_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3695\" data-vbnamecard=\"3695\">The Laughing Stranger</a> pointed above. Even if they use BSD skins, they are still unwilling victims, thus they get tainted.<br /> <br /> Another thing is that these guys are going very much above and beyond to harm their families and learn some very deep lore (Rituals 5). The Skinner scenario is a -great- source for these guys, detailing the reasons, the motives and such of how one becomes a Skin Dancer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T12:14:29-07:00","id":1111766,"title":"","content":"The Skin Dancers are not a Tribe, they are an abomination, and are not recognized as Garou by the majority of the spirits involved in the Pact (they need to learn their Gifts from other sources, like Banes). Anyway, they would not get an Ancestral Homeland because there are insufficient ancestral Skin Dancers to maintain an Ancestral Homeland (there might have been a few dozen Skin Dancers in totality, and only a dozen in existence at any given time).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T13:37:55-07:00","id":1111795,"title":"","content":"Everything that you just said (except for lack of ancestors) can be said of the Black Spirals who<i> do </i>have a homeland. The lack of ancestors are not really a problem since it's the totem that's responsible for the realm anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T13:58:02-07:00","id":1111799,"title":"","content":"But Black Spiral Dancers are a Tribe with a proper Totem (and are the most common Tribe to boot). The Skin Walkers do not have a Tribal Totem because they are not a Tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T14:03:29-07:00","id":1111802,"title":"","content":"Skin Dancers are a tribe in a technical sense. They have a totem (not sure what you are talking about) and they have gifts. There are very few of them, but numbers do not a tribe make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T15:12:38-07:00","id":1111829,"title":"","content":"Why do so many people keep forgetting Skindancer's arent a &quot;true&quot; tribe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T15:27:52-07:00","id":1111840,"title":"","content":"Minotaur is the only non-Wyrm totem that accepts Skin Walkers, it is not the Skin Walker Totem. Skin Dancers have no Rank, so they are not a Tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 07-05-2017, 06:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T16:00:11-07:00","id":1111858,"title":"","content":"There are specific skin dancer gifts, fetishes and 2 caerns...i think the entire plot of the skinner book is started because Tick is trying to steal Minotaur's place as the tribal totem of the skin dancers. So they are a tribe, but like the singing dogs they are a really small one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T17:14:45-07:00","id":1111896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1111558-skin-dancer-homeland?p=1111656#post1111656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ed Gein's spare room.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beat me to it. <br /> <br /> I was thinking some sort of crazy patchwork monstrosity of that, Moreau's House of Pain, and the realm of Clive Barker's Cenobites, done with the sort of Lovecraftian architectural geometry that can't exist in the real world and spirit denizens that look like some sort of collaboration between H.R. Giger and David Cronenberg.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T17:19:22-07:00","id":1111897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1111558-skin-dancer-homeland?p=1111760#post1111760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing is that these guys are going very much above and beyond to harm their families and learn some very deep lore (Rituals 5). The Skinner scenario is a -great- source for these guys, detailing the reasons, the motives and such of how one becomes a Skin Dancer.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are all very much walking tangles of barely repressed envy, anger, self-loathing and lust for power even before becoming spiritual Frankenstein monsters, and the addition of Rage does little to help that. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T15:50:40-07:00","id":1112385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1111558-skin-dancer-homeland?p=1111897#post1111897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They are all very much walking tangles of barely repressed envy, anger, self-loathing and lust for power even before becoming spiritual Frankenstein monsters, and the addition of Rage does little to help that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if you absolutely leave out the fact that most of them loose the envy, anger, and self-loathing once they get their power. It states that they have an epiphany of how weak they really were once they have the power. I believe that it says something else along the line of, its hard to be angry about not having something once you get it.I think that the Outcasts book gives a lot more useful information about them, as it describes that 3/4 of the tribe actually don't want to cause their kin anymore harm then they already have. Only 1 camp wants to continue doing things the way that Haight did and that is the camp featured in the Skinner SAS.<br /> <br /> To the OP, I echo Laughing Strangers original post. The closet thing they would have to a tribal homeland would be Minotaur's labyrinth right now because they haven't been around long enough to define themselves spiritually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T18:42:33-07:00","id":1112447,"title":"","content":"Skin Dancers are as Wyrm-ridden as the Black Spiral Dancers, and they do not have the excuse that they never had a chance (unlike most of the Garou born to the Black Spiral Dancers). They each deprive Gaia of five of her warriors just so they can selfishly live out their narcissistic dreams of power. They each committed the highest treason five times and need to be tossed into Erebus until the Silver Lake judges them to be pure of sin.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T20:05:52-07:00","id":1112471,"title":"","content":"Im not saying their saints, but that doesn't make them a lost cause. It also doesn't make them less of a tribe either. Lets be realistic, if they were hunting just BSD then the other tribes would look down on them sure but they wouldn't have nearly as negative an outlook. I mean the Fenrir skin themselves for fetishes and the Uktena openly dabble with dark magics that treads the line very closely. As the Skinner SAS pointed out in the end, there is a chance that Minotaur could bring them back to the Gaian side if he could get passed his own tainted being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T21:37:29-07:00","id":1112503,"title":"","content":"They are unredeemable though and, even if they skin BSD, they are irrevocably tainted by the Wyrm, paradoxically making them less excepted by their Kin than when they were Kinfolk. They are as much a part of the Wyrm as the BSD, they are just sociopaths rather than psychopaths. And they are not a Tribe because they do not possess Rank, which means that they do not have Renown and are not a part of the Pact. At least BSD have Rank, Renown, and a Pact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T04:05:44-07:00","id":1112592,"title":"","content":"Skin Dancers are people who lash out against abuse, feel they were snubbed by fate or generally just feel THEY need to take part in the fight.<br /> <br /> As for Black Spiral Dancer kin, that is actually interesting. It might be used as a carrot for really ambitious kin to join the 'big ranks' if they do well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 07-07-2017, 07:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T10:21:11-07:00","id":1112774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1111558-skin-dancer-homeland?p=1112503#post1112503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are unredeemable though and, even if they skin BSD, they are irrevocably tainted by the Wyrm, paradoxically making them less excepted by their Kin than when they were Kinfolk. They are as much a part of the Wyrm as the BSD, they are just sociopaths rather than psychopaths. And they are not a Tribe because they do not possess Rank, which means that they do not have Renown and are not a part of the Pact. At least BSD have Rank, Renown, and a Pact.</div> </div> </div> </div>You keep saying this but I don't think it matters as to whether the flensing freaks are a tribe or not. I don't think they would have rank anyway (functionally speaking) since there are so few of them. Who is going to verify your deeds before the spirits? Some other desperate skinner you never met?<br /> <br /> If groups like the Singing Dogs or the Siberakh can be weird, tiny tribes, than so can the spawn of Minotaur. They are a loose collection of werewolves that all serve the same totem and gain gifts from said totem. Sounds a lot like a tribe to me. The fact that they are not part of any greater political group, spiritual or physical, seems like a technical definition, and one I am not sure exists. Maybe they are a proto-tribe, or a bastard tribe. In any case just repeating that the Skin Dancers aren't a tribe is intensely uninteresting. They might as well be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T10:59:45-07:00","id":1112791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1111558-skin-dancer-homeland?p=1112385#post1112385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Only if you absolutely leave out the fact that most of them loose the envy, anger, and self-loathing once they get their power.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the World of Darkness, where with great power comes great corruption.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It states that they have an epiphany of how weak they really were once they have the power. I believe that it says something else along the line of, its hard to be angry about not having something once you get it. </div> </div> </div>&quot;It&quot; = ?<br /> <br /> Kinfolk go off the rails for a wide variety of reasons, many of which aren't realistically going to be resolved by the sudden achievement of physical power. And again, most of those personal issues aren't going to be improved by the sudden addition of barely controllable superhuman levels of internal fury.<br /> <br /> The Skin Dancers were conceived as the sort of thing that a group of monsters (the Garou) see as monsters (kin slayers, thieves and blasphemers), much in the same way the Diablerists are for vampires. If you want to play them as Just Like Normal Garou But Special, that's fine, but it's neutering them of a lot of their better story potential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T18:43:59-07:00","id":1113039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1111558-skin-dancer-homeland?p=1112791#post1112791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;It&quot; = ?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;It&quot; = the source material. I will clarify further:<br /> <br /> &quot;While the Skin-Dancers began in corruption, the vast majority turn away from their former ways, heading toward an inner peace brought on by their first change. For many Garou, the First Change is a traumatic experience, painful and frightening. For the Garou created by Haight, the experience was more appropriately termed an epiphany. I guess it\u2019s hard to want revenge against the people that have what you want when you suddenly get what you\u2019ve been after. The bitterness and resentment is not as strong as the Wyrm had hoped, and the Change brings forth an understanding of why the Garou considered their former Kinfolk second-class citizens. Rather than screaming, &quot;Now I can have my revenge against the bastards!&quot;, most of the Skin-Dancers respond with a sigh, &quot;Oh, I understand. They did not hate me. They pitied my lack of ability.&quot; Many among the Skin Dancers believe that Gaia retaliated against the Wyrm-spawn Samuel Haight by calming the overwhelming rage of his progeny, thus allowing them a chance at redemption despite their foul origins.&quot;<br /> --pg. 57 of &quot;Outcasts: A Players Guide to Pariah<br /> <br /> The W20 didn't include even a quarter of the information on the tribe they have given in the past. I assume this is due to space restrictions as that book was huge as it was and you don't need that information to use them in a story. If they were just a group of monsters though, then they really wouldn't be needed because you have the BSD for that. You can use them how ever you like. I am not saying otherwise. I simply choose to use all of the information the writers have contributed to the tribe; They have 4 camps, 2 caerns, 1 totem, 2 tribal gifts, 1 tribal rite, and 3 tribal fetishes. Most of the tribes numbers aren't even kinfolk that have gone through the rite. Most of their members are Ronin and Metis who are equally fed up with the treatment they have had to put up with from the Nation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T21:02:09-07:00","id":1113088,"title":"","content":"You mean a source that was written 22 years ago and two editions ago? The Skin Dancers receive adequate treatment in W20 and SAS-Skinner, and they are irredeemable in both. They killed five Garou in their selfishness, and I doubt that any Garou would be willing to forgive them. If it was not for the Apocalypse, annihilating the Skin Dancers and burning away every trace of their existence would be the number one priority for the Garou Nation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T05:49:50-07:00","id":1113694,"title":"","content":"Returning to the OP topic. Here is how I imagine the skinwalker's Homeland to look like and originate. I can be a little verbose... overwordy so please forgive me. <br /> <br /> This assumes that Homelands are distinct and separate from a spirit's realm.<br /> <br /> The spirits in the earliest nights guided the kinfolk who were skin dancers to the homeland of their tribe. The Garou, however, even in death held hatred for the skinwalkers whom they blamed for the murder and betrayal of their family, tribe and nation. The skinwalkers were hounded out of the homeland of their people. Sometimes the skinwalkers were able to carry off a piece of their homeland with them. These early spirits somehow found their way to each other, either guided by Minotaur, Owl or by chance. In a stable Pocket realm, shapeless and barren, the realm began to take shape with the stolen tidbits of other Homelands. For the longest time the realm remained sparse, almost torturous in its emptiness. <br /> <br /> Over time the Skinwalkers began to fill their homeland with purpose. The Skinwalkers developed rituals and quests which allowed them to sacrifice Caerns or significant spiritual places and items which would then ascend (descend) to skinwalker's pocket realm. Some sacrifices were the holy places of the tribes. Some skinwalkers sacrificed Spirals to remove them from the material world. Most fetishes and places, however were sacrificed in spite. As the tribe progressed and realized they were a tribe, thanks to modern communication technology, potential Elders were often given the Quest to steal directly from another nation's homeland within the umbra as a challenge for Elder Rank. The reasons could be many but the results would remain the same. The Skinwalker homeland grew into a patchwork maze made of many varying elements. Patches of dessert abutted deep dark forests. Tundra formed cliffs around deep chasms with verdant dangerous rivers below. Fetishes and Talens lay scattered in the dens of predators or created walls in a maze. This is how the Skinwalker homeland came to be. <br /> <br /> I wonder what Chiminage Minotaur paid to owl to lead his people here or if he circumvented Owl and found some other means to collect his people. <br /> <br /> \u200bJust my thoughts.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/769-chris-wilson","name":"Chris Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T06:44:10-07:00","id":1113709,"title":"","content":"The SkinDancers are not a real tribe, they are the Garou-shifting stolen to a kinfolk. They have no &quot;tribal totem&quot; and as the tribal homeland is the totem's homeland too, they have no tribal homeland - they go to erebus if they are lucky!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9729-hira-akigi","user":"Hira Akigi","date":". 07-09-2017, 10:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9729-hira-akigi","name":"Hira Akigi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T06:51:44-07:00","id":1113713,"title":"","content":"Owl is an Incarna associated with the Garou Nation, it is the Totem of the Silent Striders, so it would never help the Skin Dancers and would likely actively hunt them down during the night. The Skin Dancers just do not have the numbers or the time to do what you are suggesting.<br /> <br /> Now, if you pushed back their creation a thousand years and had the ancestral Skin Dancers interbreed with humans and wolves like the born Garou to create Kinfolk lines, then you could just have a Tribe with an unsavory past. When the Rite that created their ancestors was rediscovered, they would have been as horrified as anyone else and would sought to kill off the new Skin Dancers. In fact, that could have been the way that every new Tribe was born, just that the majority of them split off during prehistory, so the sins of their ancestors are forgotten by contemporary times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T10:46:26-07:00","id":1113790,"title":"","content":"Okay, so true, Skinwalkers are not a Tribe. They are a pseudo-tribe as per the Skinner SAS, p. 5. Still, as a pseudo-tribe I can see Skinwalkers desiring their own homeland. Fear of Erebus or some other Hell would be incentive for the few older or middle aged Skinwalkers to search for a Homeland. Considering the nature of the Skinwalkers I can't help but imagine that their homeland was stolen piece meal from other Umbral Homelands or by skinning Garou Holylands and Cairns from the Material Realm. How the Skinwalkers achieved the theft is unknown. Most likely through a rite given by Minotaur, another spirit or the Wyrm. <br /> <br /> Perhaps in the early days, Skinwalkers practiced death rites that hid their true nature from Owl, tricking the psychopomp into delivering the spirit to their tribes homeland. Once newly arrived the rite ended, leaving the Skinwalker to the not so tender mercies of the Garou who recognized them for their sins worn on their skin. <br /> <br /> This of course is all fanon. Still its fun to speculate. <br /> <br /> If the Skinwalkers were a Tribe what would their homeland look like to you?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/769-chris-wilson","name":"Chris Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T12:54:00-07:00","id":1113834,"title":"","content":"The Hell of Being Flayed Alive would be appropriate...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T12:57:23-07:00","id":1113835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1111558-skin-dancer-homeland?p=1112791#post1112791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Skin Dancers were conceived as the sort of thing that a group of monsters (the Garou) see as monsters (kin slayers, thieves and blasphemers), much in the same way the Diablerists are for vampires. If you want to play them as Just Like Normal Garou But Special, that's fine, but it's neutering them of a lot of their better story potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just going to point out one of the major playable sects runs on diab, Multiple clans have special diab friendly paths. So treating them as an acceptable but alternative take would be the same as treating them as serial diablerists in Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T13:54:28-07:00","id":1113870,"title":"","content":"But VtM is a completely different game than WtA. In VtM, everyone is a pawn of elder Kindred and the elder Kindred are fiddling while the world is burning down around them. In WtA, the Garou are the frontline in the war against the forces of the Wyrm, and traitors during wartime deserve a silver bullet in the head (the Skin Dancers are very much traitors to the Garou Nation because they each deliberately murdered five Garou so they could become Garou). There really can be no quarter given to the Skin Dancers as an active threat if the Garou wish to remain a viable force against the forces of the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T15:07:22-07:00","id":1113887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1111558-skin-dancer-homeland?p=1113870#post1113870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But VtM is a completely different game than WtA. In VtM, everyone is a pawn of elder Kindred and the elder Kindred are fiddling while the world is burning down around them. In WtA, the Garou are the frontline in the war against the forces of the Wyrm, and traitors during wartime deserve a silver bullet in the head (the Skin Dancers are very much traitors to the Garou Nation because they each deliberately murdered five Garou so they could become Garou). There really can be no quarter given to the Skin Dancers as an active threat if the Garou wish to remain a viable force against the forces of the Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes from a Garou nation perspective. From a Playability perspective treating Skindancers as a darker option since BSDs are off the table seems on par.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T15:32:43-07:00","id":1113899,"title":"","content":"You can already play a Skin Walker under W20 rules though, they are just treated as an especially nasty version of Ronin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T09:59:05-07:00","id":1114190,"title":"","content":"To Garou, Skindancers are worse than BSD. To BSD, Skindancers are just prospects. To Skindancers, Skindancers are like shining stars.<br /> <br /> But Skindancers, as a not-tribe have the same homeland problem as the Crotean, Bunyip and White Howlers: they have no homeland. Ok, the last 3 did loose their homeland, but they have none at the current point of time - and neither do they have an (uncorrupted) Totem, nor could they have anchestors.<br /> Now, what happens if they go through Erebus? They become tribeless and could be adopted by any tribe that wants.<br /> <br /> Now, how would have the Skindancer homeland looked if they had one? I don't know, but I would rule, that it has been destroyed by the Garou when they hunted them down and almost exterminated them several times. Instead, all dead Skindancers go either to Erebus to atone... or Malfeas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9729-hira-akigi","name":"Hira Akigi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T21:09:33-07:00","id":1116232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1111558-skin-dancer-homeland#post1111558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As the skin dancers are all a small tribe and every tribe has a tribal homeland according to the w20 velvet shadow book,i wanted to ask you all. What do you guys think this very fledgeling little realm would look like?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Realistically Skin Dancers do not have the infrastructure, the power base, or the resources to be able to maintain, protect, and keep secret any kind of a home base. Nor do I think Minotaur would have any intention of putting forth the effort either. Realistically they would be decentralized and some even nomadic. I don't think they'd have a homeland.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4579-skeleton-jack","name":"Skeleton Jack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T21:12:24-07:00","id":1116233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1111558-skin-dancer-homeland#post1111558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you guys think this very fledgeling little realm would look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>An giant ashtray. *ba dum dish*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T11:18:51-07:00","id":1116486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skeleton Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1111558-skin-dancer-homeland?p=1116232#post1116232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Realistically Skin Dancers do not have the infrastructure, the power base, or the resources to be able to maintain, protect, and keep secret any kind of a home base. Nor do I think Minotaur would have any intention of putting forth the effort either. Realistically they would be decentralized and some even nomadic. I don't think they'd have a homeland.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Umbral realms don't work like that. They are sort of Nomadic by nature as they connection between them change. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}